#, no-wrap
msgid "4.1 Step 1: Map {#41-step-1-map}"
msgstr "4.1 Langkah 1: Peta {#41-step-1-map}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.2 Steps 2 and 3: Optimize and Execute (Simulator) {#42-steps-2-and-3-optimize-and-execute-simulator}"
msgstr "4.2 Langkah 2 dan 3: Optimumkan dan Laksana (Simulator) {#42-steps-2-and-3-optimize-and-execute-simulator}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One user ran the next cell using a MacBook Pro with 2.3 GHz quad-core Intel Core i7 Processor equipped with 32GB 3LPDDR4X RAM, which is running macOS 14.5.  It took 161ms in wall time. Each laptop will be slightly different.\n"
msgstr "Seorang pengguna menjalankan sel seterusnya menggunakan MacBook Pro dengan pemproses Intel Core i7 2.3 GHz quad-core dilengkapi RAM 32GB 3LPDDR4X, yang menjalankan macOS 14.5. Ia mengambil masa 161ms dalam masa dinding. Setiap laptop akan sedikit berbeza.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.3 Steps 2 and 3: Optimize and execute (fake device) {#43-steps-2-and-3-optimize-and-execute-fake-device}"
msgstr "4.3 Langkah 2 dan 3: Optimumkan dan laksana (peranti palsu) {#43-steps-2-and-3-optimize-and-execute-fake-device}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the same user ran the next cell with the same environment as above, it took 2min 19s in Wall Time.  Executing a circuit on a fake device invokes noisy simulation which takes much longer time than exact simulation.   We recommend you not execute a larger circuit (such as a 27-qubit $\\times$ 9 layers with 3 Trotter steps) on a fake device.\n"
msgstr "Apabila pengguna yang sama menjalankan sel seterusnya dengan persekitaran yang sama seperti di atas, ia mengambil masa 2 minit 19 saat dalam Masa Dinding. Melaksanakan litar pada peranti palsu menggunakan simulasi berbising yang mengambil masa jauh lebih lama daripada simulasi tepat. Kami mengesyorkan anda tidak melaksanakan litar yang lebih besar (seperti litar 27-qubit $\\times$ 9 lapisan dengan 3 langkah Trotter) pada peranti palsu.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.4 Step 4: Post-process {#44-step-4-post-process}"
msgstr "4.4 Langkah 4: Pasca-proses {#44-step-4-post-process}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We plot the results from exact and noisy simulations. You see the severe effects of noise on FakeToronto.\n"
msgstr "Kita memplot hasil daripada simulasi tepat dan berbising. Anda dapat melihat kesan teruk bunyi pada FakeToronto.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/utility-i/extracted-outputs/4cf3cad0-e720-469c-a9ed-e397dae0f2f6-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/utility-i/extracted-outputs/4cf3cad0-e720-469c-a9ed-e397dae0f2f6-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Solve the 127-qubit version of the problem {#5-solve-the-127-qubit-version-of-the-problem}"
msgstr "5. Selesaikan versi 127-qubit bagi masalah ini {#5-solve-the-127-qubit-version-of-the-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is your goal to run the utility-scale experiment as mentioned at the beginning. You will create and execute a 127-qubit and 60-layer (20 Trotter steps) circuit with  $\\langle Z_{62} \\rangle$ as an observable. We recommend you try to do this yourself, using the code for the 27-qubit version when appropriate. But the solution is provided here.\n"
msgstr "Matlamat anda adalah untuk menjalankan eksperimen berskala utility seperti yang disebutkan pada awalnya. Anda akan mencipta dan melaksanakan litar 127 qubit dan 60 lapisan (20 langkah Trotter) dengan $\\langle Z_{62} \\rangle$ sebagai observable. Kami mengesyorkan anda cuba melakukan ini sendiri, menggunakan kod untuk versi 27-qubit apabila sesuai. Tetapi penyelesaiannya disediakan di sini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "__Solution:__\n"
msgstr "__Penyelesaian:__\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "5.1 Step 1: Map {#51-step-1-map}"
msgstr "5.1 Langkah 1: Peta {#51-step-1-map}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "5.2 Steps 2 and 3: Optimize and execute {#52-steps-2-and-3-optimize-and-execute}"
msgstr "5.2 Langkah 2 dan 3: Optimumkan dan laksana {#52-steps-2-and-3-optimize-and-execute}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We note that the coupling map of the Eagle processor has 144 edges.\n"
msgstr "Kita perhatikan bahawa peta gandingan pemproses Eagle mempunyai 144 tepi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "5.3 Post-process {#53-post-process}"
msgstr "5.3 Pasca-proses {#53-post-process}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We provide the values for the \"mitigated\" points in Figure 4b of the utility paper.   Plot these together with your results.\n"
msgstr "Kita menyediakan nilai untuk titik \"yang telah dikurangkan kesalahannya\" dalam Rajah 4b kertas utility. Plot nilai-nilai ini bersama hasil anda.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/utility-i/extracted-outputs/1c4ede0c-e865-41fe-9b38-8ecf39afa64f-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/utility-i/extracted-outputs/1c4ede0c-e865-41fe-9b38-8ecf39afa64f-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Are your results similar to the \"unmitigated\" in Figure 4b? &nbsp; They could be very different, depending on the device and its condition at the time of experiment.  Do not worry about the results themselves. What we will check is whether you have done the coding correctly.  If you have done so, congratulations, you have reached the starting line of the utility era.\n"
msgstr "Adakah hasil anda serupa dengan \"yang tidak dikurangkan kesalahannya\" dalam Rajah 4b? &nbsp; Ia mungkin sangat berbeza, bergantung pada peranti dan keadaannya semasa eksperimen. Jangan bimbang tentang hasil itu sendiri. Apa yang akan kita semak ialah sama ada anda telah melakukan pengekodan dengan betul. Jika anda telah melakukannya, tahniah, anda telah mencapai garis permulaan era utility.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As in the Utility paper, scientists across the globe have put forth tremendous ingenuity to extracting meaningful results even in the presence of noise. The end goal of this collective effort is quantum advantage: a state in which quantum computers can solve some problems of use in industry faster, with higher fidelity, or more cheaply than classical computers. This is not likely to be a single event, but rather an era in which classical reproduction of quantum results takes progressively longer, until at some point that quantum lead time becomes critically important. One thing is clear about quantum advantage: we get there only through the utility-scale experiments.  If this course results in your joining the quest, which is full of challenge and fun, we would be more than happy.\n"
msgstr "Seperti dalam kertas Utility, para saintis di seluruh dunia telah menunjukkan kreativiti yang luar biasa untuk mengekstrak hasil yang bermakna walaupun dalam kehadiran bunyi. Matlamat akhir usaha bersama ini ialah kelebihan kuantum: suatu keadaan di mana komputer kuantum dapat menyelesaikan beberapa masalah yang berguna dalam industri dengan lebih pantas, dengan ketepatan lebih tinggi, atau lebih murah berbanding komputer klasik. Ini berkemungkinan bukan peristiwa tunggal, tetapi lebih kepada suatu era di mana penghasilan semula klasik bagi hasil kuantum mengambil masa yang semakin lama, sehingga pada satu ketika masa unggul kuantum itu menjadi sangat penting. Satu perkara yang jelas tentang kelebihan kuantum: kita hanya boleh sampai ke sana melalui eksperimen berskala utility. Jika kursus ini mengakibatkan anda menyertai pencarian ini, yang penuh cabaran dan keseronokan, kami akan sangat gembira.\n"

